# Shipped code is gated at level 5 — the first level that reports argument
# type mismatches, which is the check most worth having here. src/ passes
# it clean.
#
# tests/ is gated at 2 via a second pass because one helper blocks 3 and
# up: HttpsSinkTest::clientWith() hands an array by reference to Guzzle's
# Middleware::history(), whose container is untyped and inferred as
# array|ArrayAccess<int, array>. By-ref parameters must match the callee
# exactly, so closing it means widening the helper's own signature to
# accept an ArrayAccess it is never called with. Fold tests/ back into the
# level 5 run above once that helper is retyped; nothing else in tests/
# fails at 5.
#
# Level 6 would cost 3 errors in src/ (missing iterable value types).
#
# No baseline and no ignore list: every error reported here is a real one.
parameters:
    level: 5
    paths:
        - src
